#### Auth:

1. IAM

T&F's internal system for managing who can access what. For an institution to use your app, you create a **service account** in IAM. This service account has credentials your backend uses to call T&F's content API on behalf of the institution's users.
    
    **For the app itself — two token types:**
    
    Roughly:
    
    - **User token** — proves who the person is (their identity)
    - **Access token** — proves what they're allowed to do (their entitlement)
    
    ```java
    1. User signs in
            │
            ▼
    Identity Provider / IDAM
    (Authentication)
            │
            ▼
    JWT Access Token issued
            │
            ▼
    User requests "Mining Handbook.epub"
            │
            ▼
    Backend validates the JWT
            │
            ▼
    Backend checks subscription and entitlements
    (Authorization)
            │
            ▼
    Backend uses its Service Account (created in IDAM)
    to call the internal Content API
            │
            ▼
    Content API confirms the institution has access
            │
            ▼
    Backend generates a pre-signed URL
            │
            ▼
    User downloads the EPUB directly from cloud storage
    ```
    
